-In the multiwave recovery example, weekly deaths equal their model expectations, so the first observed hazard gives the generating baseline rate exactly. With that rate fixed, the example checks recovery of the enrollment-time frailty variance and alignment of the quiet windows. The synthetic negative control also checks whether KCOR remains near 1 under a true null effect. Near-1 behavior in this setting is treated as a diagnostic implication of correct working-model alignment, not as a stand-alone proof of estimator validity. Full design details, recovery grids, and figures are provided in the Supplementary Information, including the $\theta_0$ recovery simulations and the synthetic negative-control figures (Section S4.2.1 and related figures).
